## 4. Qualified public evidence and currentness

The only positive threshold data root is an accepted `SyntheticEligibilityAssessmentV21` from the exact2.1 source profile introduced by scientific5409, with the qualified public binary measurement and exact obligation/episode/source-prefix semantics. If final accepted2.1 fields differ, this proposal requires a reviewed mapping revision before implementation; no guessed field extraction. False/unknown/absent/not-applicable/malformed status is never satisfaction of an open threshold obligation. A true binary plus inconsistent per-obligation status is rejected as source inconsistency. A public trigger fact that a hold occurred is not a positive assessment.

No numerical L, hidden U, private seed, evaluator truth, posterior estimate, wearable score, ISI improvement, burden score, raw pain value, generated `requirements_satisfied` review, archive resolution or archived owner assertion may substitute. The live service reads only qualified public products. Upstream measurement likelihood is applied once by scientific consumers; live review/journal descendants supply provenance, not a second independent measurement. This proposal does not implement or audit a private generator/evaluator.

Define `source-current` at live review receipt C as all of:

1. The policy/grant and source acceptance are active under exact persisted common control. Owner/patient/run/partition/episode mappings resolve uniquely. Root assessment schema/law/measurement source match the policy, and its explicit assessed local date/time and episode/generation/obligation entries cover every relevant threshold trigger. An archive generation number is not the live generation; the persisted admission mapping connects them exactly.
2. Read the original assessment, raw payload/hash, manifest, source-prefix closure and all recursively referenced source facts from **already committed** storage under the admission gate. Each source event/recorded/effective-available clock is <=C; no future source fact or same-transaction evidence insert qualifies. Save actual committed read proof at C and supplying receipt, not inferred first-publication time. Repeat after acquiring the SQLite writer and before commit.
3. Its source assessment order is at or after the latest threshold trigger occurrence it purports to cover, by exact source event time and declared source causal sequence where equality is legal. It must use the current nonretracted lineage head for each dependency. A later corrective version of the same event does not invent a later assessment. A newer actual trigger, conflicting assessment, correction, retraction, source-prefix amendment, ownership/control change or new required item invalidates current consideration. Cycles, cross-patient receipt chains and missing recursive leaves reject.
4. The accepted source-prefix closure explicitly lists the complete applicable public assessment and safety-record set through its declared source cutoff and exact package-series revision. The live coordinator has admitted all positive requires-hold facts in that committed prefix; mere archive import does not suffice. Current DB safety journal/control high-water marks match the review snapshot. A committed new package/prefix with a later relevant fact cannot be ignored by choosing an older true assessment. Across permitted package revisions, choose the uniquely latest accepted applicable assessment; conflicting/ambiguous heads stay pending. This is a completeness assertion of the qualified synthetic source over a finite prefix, not a claim that future observations cannot arrive.
5. Qualified observed alive/outpatient status and exact admission/discharge/death lineage at the same complete source cutoff do not indicate death or ongoing admission. Missing or contradictory status is pending. An original admission episode elsewhere is not cleared by these facts; its own live latch remains. Remaining consent, protocol, regimen, medication exclusions and participant pauses stay independent authoritative constraints. Unsupported related obligations within the selected episode still block its whole clearance.

**Freshness choice:** There is deliberately no clinical maximum-age interval and no rule `service_today == simulated_assessment_day`. The live operator assesses the exact current *synthetic replay prefix now*, with original source date and present C displayed. The rule does not claim the old simulated patient is clinically stable at wall-clock C. No auto-forwarding of a date, “fresh” label based only on ingestion, or silent inclusion of unavailable data. If true real-time clinical freshness is requested, CLINICAL-CLEARANCE-01 must provide a separately accepted rule; this profile cannot serve it. This choice is essential for replay feasibility and must be explicitly accepted by the independent critic/root.

